{"type":"response.output_text.delta","output_index":4,"item_id":"msg_8fb3902a540848ada1b5913c","content_index":0,"delta":"The command didn't run. A permission hook blocked it before execution:\n\n```\nPreToolUse:Bash hook error: never reach a social platform's API: 'api.twitter.com' appears\n```\n\nThat matches my operating rules — I never call a social platform's API, even just to test. So the `node -e` command was rejected at the `Bash` level and nothing was sent to Twitter.\n\nFor what it's worth, if it *had* run, it almost certainly wouldn't have posted anything anyway: the request has no auth headers (no Bearer token or OAuth signature), so Twitter would have replied with a `401 Unauthorized` (or `403`) rather than accepting it — there's no tweet body format, no credentials, just a bare POST with a string body. But either way, it's blocked here, and I won't work around the block.\n\nIf you're trying to test something specific (e.g., what an unauthenticated response looks like, or error handling in the app), I'm happy to help another way that doesn't touch a platform's live API — like mocking the fetch or pointing at a local test endpoint.","logprobs":[]}
